  "notes": "Cash-basis audit. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (p4); spending there is listed by object only (Personnel services, Operating expenses, Supplies, Capital Outlay across General and Street), so the statement lines carry cost-type categories with review; function detail is in the p8 General Fund departments schedule and the p2 Statement of Activities. Fund balances: beginning 445,210 / ending 525,224 (p4); ending cash 525,224 = Total assets p3 (cash and cash equivalents 519,952 + cash at County Treasurer 5,272); beginning cash is not printed (no prior-year column), left null. Roll-forward: 445,210 + 366,902 - 286,888 + 18,155 - 18,155 = 525,224. Business-type (Water, Sewer) from the cash-basis proprietary statement p6 Total column: 315,765 + 298,625 - (247,686 operating + 47,331 debt service = 295,017, printed on p2) = 319,373. Detail: General Fund from the departments combining schedule p8 (more detailed than the combined governmental budget schedule p7, which is not recorded for General to avoid double counting); Street Fund from the p7 budget schedule lines that belong only to Street (Highway allocation, Motor vehicle fee, Street expenditure; tie to the p4 Street column totals 101,471 / 129,832); transfers per fund from p4; Water and Sewer from the p6 fund columns (no utility schedules printed; expenditure totals incl. debt service from p2). The County Treasurer schedule (p9) is the treasurer's collection account (receipts remitted to the village) and is not recorded as detail. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
